Cleaned raw data for 800+ companies worldwide using SQL, then built an interactive 
 Power BI dashboard showing layoff trends by company, industry, country, and time.

Data Cleaning (SQL)
Created staging tables and preserved an original copy of the data.
Removed duplicates using ROW_NUMBER() OVER(PARTITION BY...).
Standardized company names, country names, and industry categories (e.g. unifying "Crypto" variants).
Converted the date column from text to DATE, handled nulls via self-join, and dropped rows with no analytical value.

Exploratory Analysis
Monthly rolling total of layoffs using a Window Function.
Ranked the top 5 companies by layoffs each year using DENSE_RANK().

Key Findings
The "Finance" sector recorded the highest number of layoff events.
Amazon, Google, and Ericsson topped the list of companies by total employees laid off.
2022 accounted for the highest share of total layoffs at 41.66%.
